# Secrets — NEVER version
.secrets.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Money/business docs — NOT in the shared repo (a teammate pulls and would see them)
PROPUESTA-LEO.md
PROPUESTA-LEO.docx
NEGOCIO/

# Literature — INDEX.md + FICHAS.md are tracked; the PDFs themselves are not.
# See the two literature blocks below.

# Data / weights / checkpoints (live on RunPod, not here)
data/
datasets/
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
checkpoints/
external_data/

# Run artifacts stay out (weights, predictions, logs — they live on RunPod).
# EXCEPTION: the canonical `stratified.json` IS versioned. A few KB of pure JSON, no
# weights. Reason: `results/` is COMMITTED but `frame.ledger.build_results_ledger`
# regenerates it from these files. With them ignored, rebuilding on a clone that lacks
# another run's artifacts silently DOWNGRADES that run's committed row to
# needs_backfill=True with every floor/margin → NaN (verified 2026-07-18: a rebuild
# here wiped 02-lora-sft's and 00-baseline's canonical margins). Versioning them is
# what makes the ledger's "auto-built, cannot drift" promise true on ANY clone.
# NOTE: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT directory is excluded, so these
# patterns exclude the run CONTENTS and re-include the directories to descend through.
runs/**
experiments/*/runs/**
experiments_segment/*/runs/**
!runs/**/
!experiments/*/runs/**/
!experiments_segment/*/runs/**/
!runs/**/stratified.json
!experiments/*/runs/**/stratified.json
!experiments_segment/*/runs/**/stratified.json
wandb/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Obsidian — local editor config (the vault IS the repo; .md files are versioned, the workspace isn't)
.obsidian/

# Literature PDFs of the technique corpora — the INDEX.md/FICHAS.md ARE the artifact.
# 664 MB / 87 files (preprocessing 396 MB, vlm-techniques 268 MB). PDFs are already
# compressed, so git gains nothing from delta/zlib: committing them takes .git from
# 167 MB to ~830 MB and a fresh clone to ~1.5 GB, crossing GitHub's 1 GB soft warning,
# and one file (p04_awad_2025) is 81 MB — past the 50 MB warning, 19 MB short of the
# 100 MB hard reject. Git-LFS is worse: its free tier is 1 GB storage + 1 GB/month
# bandwidth, so three clones exhaust the quota in month one. Every catalogued paper
# carries an arXiv/PMC link and a byte-verified status column, so the PDFs are
# reconstructible on demand.
# 🔻 Updated 2026-09-09: the 21 PDFs in literature/pdfs/ used to be tracked, on the
# reasoning that this was a PRIVATE repo and a teammate needed them. The repo is now
# public, so they are untracked too (see the PUBLIC REPO block at the bottom). They
# remain in the git HISTORY — evicting them needs a force-push the whole team agrees to.
literature/preprocessing/pdfs/
literature/vlm-techniques/pdfs/

# UNAM HPC cluster access — SSH public keys sent to the sysadmin for the ENES
# Juriquilla server. Personal access material, not project code: the keys are
# per-person, they grant nothing on their own, and a teammate has their own pair.
# Nothing here is reproducible from the repo, so nothing here belongs in it.
UNAM/

# Junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Human-adjudication staging (rung 16b follow-up). Challenge frames are COPIES of
# /workspace/frames_cache pixels -- the single-source rule says a frame exists once and is
# called from there, never duplicated into the repo. The instrument itself is versioned at
# experiments/16-count-probes/_tools/contar.html; only this scratch copy is ignored.
local/adjudicate/

# Submission packages: the recipe is versioned, the 17 GB of merged weights and the
# built tarball are not. `submissions/<id>/README.md` documents how to regenerate both.
submissions/*/resources/
submissions/*/test/
submissions/*/*.tar.gz
submissions/*/__pycache__/

# Build artifacts for a submission: a 17 GB image tar and 33.5 GB of FP8 weights.
# They are REPRODUCIBLE (buildah on UNAM + a 32 s re-quantization from the 323 MB adapter),
# and 50 GB of binaries in a git history is not a mistake you undo.
submissions/*/_artifacts/

# local agent scratch — never repo content
.claude/worktrees/
.codex/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC REPO (since 2026-09) — everything below is on disk but NOT exposed.
# Untracked with `git rm --cached`: the files stay on every machine, git just
# stops publishing them. Nothing here is needed to read the method.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Personal working vault (legokna). It is an INDEPENDENT git repository with its
# own history, deliberately isolated from this one — its contents were never at
# risk of being versioned here. This line is belt-and-braces: it was excluded via
# .git/info/exclude, which is per-clone and does not travel, so a clone elsewhere
# could still record an accidental gitlink. Now it cannot.
local/


# Superseded handoff note, kept on disk for the record.
HANDOFF_RUNG19.md


# Third-party papers. The catalogue (INDEX.md / FICHAS.md) IS the artifact and
# stays tracked; every entry carries an arXiv/PMC link. Redistributing 146 MB of
# other people's PDFs from a public repo is not ours to do.
literature/pdfs/

# Every PDF in the tree: the organizers' challenge documents (theirs to distribute,
# not ours) and the three literature corpora. Catalogues stay, PDFs do not.
*.pdf

# Frames from the challenge corpus. Patient-derived surgical imagery under the
# ORENA DUA — a public repo is not a permitted redistribution channel.
_presentation_frames/
